<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεμ-βολή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>insertion, interpolation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτέρων πραγμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.205
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.166
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.261
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm.,
			<i>parenthesis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tib.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				48
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>drawing up in battle-order</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				11.32.6
			</span></i> ; in Tactics, <i>insertion of men in the ranks</i> (dist.
			fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρένταξις</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεμπλοκή</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>company</i> of soldiers, etc., <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				32.2(3)
			</span></i> ; <i>host</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				33.8
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Ezek.
				<u>Exag.</u>
				81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>encampment</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theophil.
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Crito Com.
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				14.19
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.74.5
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				27
			</span></i> : generally, <i>soldiers' quarters</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.29.1
			</span></i> ; <i>barracks,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Act.Ap.
				21.34
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ostr.</u>
				901
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span> ; name of an <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμφοδον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				2131.8
			</span></i><span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεξειρεσία</span>
			 (q. v.), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.7.4
			</span></i> (sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραβολαί</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in boxing and
			wrestling, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. βάλλειν</span>
			<i>trip</i> an adversary by a twist of the leg, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Ocyp.</u>
				60
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.638f
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
